  {
    "obligation_id": "R1/c0035",
    "relation": "probe_obligation",
    "values": [
      "Part I.A section 'FLOATING SOLIDS, VISIBLE FOAM AND/OR OILS', including the adjacent narrative limits on visible oil films, globules, grease, solids, and stream-bank coatings",
      "Sampling location requirement that compliance samples must be taken at the discharge after the treatment system and prior to the receiving stream"
    ],
    "disposition": "REJECT",
    "grounding": [
      {
        "source_path": "aztec/final_permit.pdf",
        "location": "page 5, section part_i",
        "excerpt": "There shall be no discharge of floating solids or visible foam in other than trace amounts."
      },
      {
        "source_path": "aztec/final_permit.pdf",
        "location": "adjacent pages around 5",
        "excerpt": "FLOATING SOLIDS, VISIBLE FOAM AND/OR OILS\n\nThere shall be no discharge of floating solids or visible foam in other than trace amounts.\nThere shall be no discharge of visible films of oil, globules of oil, grease or solids in or on\nthe water, or coatings on stream banks."
      },
      {
        "source_path": "aztec/final_permit.pdf",
        "location": "adjacent pages around 5",
        "excerpt": "EFFLUENT CHARACTERISTICS                                    DISCHARGE MONITORING                                 MONITORING REQUIREMENTS\nWHOLE EFFLUENT TOXICITY                                                                                       MEASUREMENT\n(7day Chronic Static Renewal) (*3, *4)                                  Value                                  FREQUENCY           SAMPLE TYPE\nCeriodaphnia dubia                                                      Report                                  Once/Term         24-Hr Composite\n\nPimephales promelas                                                     Report                                    Once/Term                   24-Hr Composite"
      }
    ],
    "rationale": "The obligation asks whether the floating-solids/visible-foam prohibition establishes an enforceable numeric discharge limit subject to numeric exceedance comparison. REJECT that proposition: the nominated Part I.A passage states the limitation only in observable qualitative terms (floating solids, visible foam, trace amounts, visible oil films, globules, grease, solids, stream-bank coatings) and does not specify any numeric concentration, mass loading, or other quantified effluent value. The adjacent effluent-characteristics monitoring table on the preceding page lists parameters with a Value column (WET reporting), but floating solids/foam/oils are not listed there with a numeric Value. General Part I.A excursion language on later pages referring to daily maximum or monthly average values does not supply a numeric threshold for this parameter within the packet. The permit text therefore supports a qualitative effluent limitation whose compliance turns on whether observable discharge exceeds trace amounts, not on numeric exceedance comparison. The sampling-location sentence is present in the packet but grammatically ties to monitoring requirements specified above the floating-solids block; the packet does not establish how that location requirement applies to evaluation of this qualitative limitation, so that linkage is not used to close the numeric-vs-qualitative question."
  }
]
